{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107162","id":2570796564,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6ZOz4U","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107162","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107162.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107162.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107162","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107162/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107162/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107162/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/3e0212fc364a2e88e6f26eda594ba6aa67f6c8fe","number":107162,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"De-duplicate hash entry erase in `HashMap` and `AHashMap`","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`HashMap` and `AHashMap` currently use the same code in `erase` and `replace_key`. The code isn't trivial, so having it duplicated increases maintenance burden.\r\n\r\nI used the opportunity to fix a few other small oddities:\r\n- I exchanged one use of `fastmod` to `increment_mod`, which is faster.\r\n- Elements are no longer swapped to their predecessor. Instead, they are only propagated backwards, eliminating half of the write calls.\r\n- Checks in `erase` for `head_element` and `tail_element` were essentially performed twice. I consolidated the checks.\r\n- `_insert_element` in `HashMap` previously incremented `num_elements`, which was needed only for one of 3 callers. I moved the incrementing instead to the caller.\r\n\r\n## Benchmarks\r\n\r\nI checked performance for `erase`. It is, on average, 3% faster after the change (hot hash map):\r\n```c++\r\n\tfor (int size : { 1, 2, 8, 64, 1024, 4096, 20000}) {\r\n\t\t{\r\n\t\t\tsize_t time_ns = 0;\r\n\t\t\tfor (int run = 0; run < 20000000 / size; run++) {\r\n\t\t\t\tHashMap<Variant, Variant, VariantHasher, VariantComparator> dictionary;\r\n\t\t\t\tfor (int idx = 0; idx < size; idx ++) {\r\n\t\t\t\t\t// Test\r\n\t\t\t\t\tdictionary.insert(idx, idx);\r\n\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t\tauto t0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\t\t\tfor (int idx = 0; idx < size; idx ++) {\r\n\t\t\t\t\t// Test\r\n\t\t\t\t\tdictionary.erase(idx);\r\n\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t\tauto t1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\r\n\t\t\t\ttime_ns += std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::nanoseconds>(t1 - t0).count();\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\r\n\t\t\tstd::cout << \"erase:\" << size << std::endl;\r\n\t\t\tstd::cout << time_ns / 1000 / 1000 << \"ms\\n\";\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t}\r\n```","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2304948121,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMzA0OTQ4MTIx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:codestyle","name":"topic:codestyle","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":5793,"closed_issues":0,"created_at":"2022-07-26T12:42:05Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T14:39:14Z","closed_at":null,"due_on":null},"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2025-06-05T16:13:16Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T20:10:24Z","closed_at":null,"